From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:26:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 47/49] Dispersive line hooks a z-vector at a time,
 coefficients apart from the state

The packed hooks of the Lorentz / Drude and Debye extensions grouped
four consecutive positions of an x-line. In a filled block those are
four z of one column, that is four f4vectors with one lane each: every
group gathered and scattered scalars through twelve float indices, and
its block held coefficients and state together, so the whole block was
read and written back each timestep (about 132 bytes a Lorentz cell and
156 a Debye cell, against 49 for a plain cell).

A group is now the positions of one f4vector (base offset and lane
mask; masked lanes keep their field bits) whenever a hook has at least
2.5 positions a group on average; thin structures such as conducting
sheets keep the position groups. The coefficients live in a table of
distinct sets with an index a group (16 or 32 bit, or a record a group
when nearly every group differs), apart from the state that is written.
The per-position arrays are freed after packing. The arithmetic of each
lane is unchanged, so results stay bit-identical.

OPENEMS_ADE_VEC=0 keeps the position groups, 2 forces vector groups;
OPENEMS_ADE_COEF=group|table|table32 picks the coefficient layout
(both for tests).

Checked bit-identical: 630 box configurations (lanes 4, 3, 2, 1 and a
split mask, both group kinds, every coefficient layout, y bands, tiled
box mode, 1 to 6 threads), the dispersive check against stock at 50 k
and 1 M cells, the closed cylinder, the six harness models, the Debye
check and the validation suite.

Mac Studio (M5 Max), upstream bench.py with a source, dispersive case,
18 threads, MC/s before -> after: 30 M cells 2108 -> 2962, 8 M cells
2068 -> 2976, 1 M cells 2777 -> 3942; memory at 30 M cells 6580 ->
5857 MiB. Antenna case 0.99 to 1.02 at every size; the two boards
(conducting sheets, position groups) 1.005 at 18 threads.

